# Appearance · Composer · "Tool, thinking and delivery chips". On, a
# conversation that has never chosen a fold starts with its tool rows OPEN;
# a fold chosen in a conversation always wins over the default. rfold's
# fixture has two tool piles whose outputs are hidden when folded.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":1000,"open_tabs":[],"active_tab":"","theme":"dark","disclosure_chips_open":true}
# env: HANABI_FOLD_DEMO=1 HANABI_OPEN=rfold
require_thread rfold
wait_frames 12
# The default is ON and rfold chose nothing: both piles are open.
expect_text "182 cache/evict.rs"
expect_text "lru_drops_the_oldest_entry_first"

# Choose Fold IN this conversation: the per-thread choice wins immediately...
click_ui composer_fold
wait_frames 8
click_ui fold_row_0
wait_frames 12
expect_no_text "182 cache/evict.rs"
expect_no_text "lru_drops_the_oldest_entry_first"

# ...and keeps winning after the default is switched off and on again.
click_ui sb_settings
wait_frames 16
click_ui sb_settings_nav_appearance
wait_frames 12
expect_text "Composer"
click_ui settings_disclosure_chips
wait_frames 8
click_ui settings_disclosure_chips
wait_frames 8
click_ui tab_close
wait_frames 12
expect_open rfold
expect_no_text "182 cache/evict.rs"
